# Cascadia env-var template — copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   $ cp .env.example .env
#   $ source .env
#   $ ./target/release/cascadia-proxy
#
# Only `CASCADIA_OPENAI_API_KEY` (or any one provider key) is strictly
# required; the others are optional and gain you more upstreams. Everything
# else has a sensible default if unset — see crates/proxy/src/config.rs for
# the resolution order.

# ─── Proxy listen address ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev defaults to 0.0.0.0:8080. Cloud platforms (Railway, Render,
# Heroku) inject $PORT — the proxy reads that as a fallback.
# CASCADIA_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080

# ─── Upstream provider credentials ───────────────────────────────────────
# At least one of these is required. The model strings in your policy file
# select which one is used per cluster (e.g. `openai/gpt-4o-mini`).
CASCADIA_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# CASCADIA_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CASCADIA_GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# CASCADIA_XAI_API_KEY=xai-...

# Optional base-URL overrides — point at private endpoints (vLLM, Mistral,
# DeepSeek, Together, …) without changing code. See docs/adding-a-provider.md.
# CASCADIA_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com
# CASCADIA_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# CASCADIA_GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai
# CASCADIA_XAI_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai

# ─── Standalone live demo (scripts/quickstart.sh CASCADIA_LIVE=1) ─────────
# Drives REAL traffic through a real cascade and scores it with a real
# multi-model judge panel — spends real API budget. The judge panel must be a
# DIFFERENT family than the cascade (anti-self-preference). Keys are read from
# the plain provider env vars below (NOT the CASCADIA_-prefixed ones the proxy
# uses), since the judge poller + LLM-panel call providers directly.
# CASCADIA_LIVE=1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...          # cascade (Haiku -> Sonnet) + proxy
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...                 # cross-family judge panel
# CASCADIA_CHEAP_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5
# CASCADIA_EXPENSIVE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
# CASCADIA_JUDGE_PANEL=openai:gpt-4o-mini,openai:gpt-4o   # default from judge_ensemble.json
# CASCADIA_LIVE_SHADOW_RATE=0.5         # fraction mirrored to expensive for judging
# CASCADIA_JUDGE_BASE_URL=              # override the judge endpoint for ALL clients
#   (cascadia-judge-poll --base-url). Point the judge at a local mock/gateway —
#   e.g. http://mock-upstream:18081/v1 in the keyless `npx cascadia demo` stack,
#   where a dummy OPENAI_API_KEY + the mock = judging with no real keys or cost.

# ─── Bearer-token auth on /v1/* (recommended for public proxy deploys) ───
# Unset = open access; set to a random string to require Authorization:
# Bearer <token> on every chat-completion request.
# CASCADIA_PROXY_BEARER_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 24)

# ─── Postgres event log ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, events are logged via tracing but not persisted; the
# dashboard's Pareto chart will be empty.
CASCADIA_DATABASE_URL=postgres://cascadia:cascadia@localhost:5432/cascadia

# ─── Cascade routing policy ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# CASCADIA_POLICY_FILE — path to a JSON policy file. Hot-reloaded by the
# proxy on file change. See README "Quick start" + docs/adding-a-provider.md
# for the format.
# CASCADIA_POLICY_FILE=/tmp/cascadia-policy.json
#
# CASCADIA_POLICY_JSON — inline JSON, used by deploy targets without a
# writable volume (Railway, Render, Fly). Either FILE or JSON works.
# CASCADIA_POLICY_JSON={"default_cluster":"default","cluster_buckets":4,"clusters":{...}}
#
# CASCADIA_POLICY_SOURCE — where the proxy reads its (hot-reloadable) policy:
#   json (default) | file | postgres. Use `postgres` to close the
#   policy-controller -> proxy loop on deploys where a shared volume can't be
#   mounted into both services (Railway): the controller appends to the shared
#   `policy_store` table and the proxy polls + hot-swaps. On first boot with an
#   empty table the proxy seeds row 1 from CASCADIA_POLICY_JSON.
# CASCADIA_POLICY_SOURCE=postgres
# CASCADIA_POLICY_POLL_SECS=5   # proxy poll interval for the postgres source
#
# CASCADIA_CLUSTER_BUCKETS — number of classifier buckets. Set if you're
# running a multi-cluster policy via env-var-only (no file).
# CASCADIA_CLUSTER_BUCKETS=4
#
# ─── Policy controller (auto-tuning) ─────────────────────────────────────
# The controller refits each cluster's threshold toward a target judge score.
# Set CASCADIA_POLICY_SOURCE=postgres on the controller too so it reads/writes
# the shared policy_store. All UpdateRule knobs are env-overridable (handy to
# make a demo visibly tune without a code change):
# CASCADIA_REFIT_INTERVAL_SEC=300     # seconds between refits
# CASCADIA_LOOKBACK_MINUTES=60        # stats window
# CASCADIA_REFIT_TARGET=0.5           # target P(cheap >= expensive)
# CASCADIA_REFIT_MARGIN=0.05          # dead-band around target
# CASCADIA_REFIT_STEP=0.03            # threshold step per refit
# CASCADIA_REFIT_MIN_SAMPLE_SIZE=20   # min judged scores before tuning a cluster
# CASCADIA_REFIT_MIN_THRESHOLD=0.3
# CASCADIA_REFIT_MAX_THRESHOLD=0.95

# ─── Data residency ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CASCADIA_PERSIST_BODIES — store verbatim request/response bodies in the
# events table. Off by default; turn on for full closed-loop quality
# scoring when your traffic is PII-free.
# CASCADIA_PERSIST_BODIES=false
#
# CASCADIA_REDACT_SHADOW_BODIES — SHA-256 the shadow_pairs text columns
# instead of storing verbatim. For regulated environments; disables the
# judge's ability to score quality. See SECURITY.md for the trade-off.
# CASCADIA_REDACT_SHADOW_BODIES=false

# ─── Telemetry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CASCADIA_LOG_LEVEL=info             # trace | debug | info | warn | error
# CASCADIA_LOG_JSON=true              # JSON log lines for production
# CASCADIA_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318/v1/traces

# ─── Graceful shutdown ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CASCADIA_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECS=30   # K8s default — match terminationGracePeriodSeconds

# ─── Dashboard-api (separate service) ────────────────────────────────────
# CASCADIA_DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0
# CASCADIA_DASHBOARD_PORT=18082
# CASCADIA_DASHBOARD_API_BASE=http://localhost:18082   # Next.js → dashboard-api
# CASCADIA_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:8080             # dashboard-api → proxy
# CASCADIA_DASHBOARD_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# ─── Operator dashboard auth (email + password) ──────────────────────────
# The dashboard gates the operator UI behind first-class email/password
# accounts (PLAN.md §9, 2026-06-01). Accounts + opaque server-side sessions
# live in the dashboard-api/Postgres; the Next.js middleware validates the
# session cookie against dashboard-api on every gated request. There are no
# secrets to set for auth itself — accounts are created via the /signup page.
#
# Local-dev escape hatch: bypass the gate when running the Next UI without the
# Python backend. Honored ONLY when NODE_ENV != production.
# CASCADIA_AUTH_DISABLED=true
#
# Seal signup: refuse new accounts (403) on instances you don't want strangers
# joining — e.g. a public demo deploy. Default open (local/self-host onboarding
# is unchanged). The first/bootstrap account is always allowed even when sealed,
# so a fresh instance can't lock itself out. Set on the dashboard-api service.
# CASCADIA_SIGNUP_DISABLED=true
#
# Email confirmation: signup is double opt-in — the account stays unverified
# (can't log in) until the emailed link is clicked. With no SMTP configured the
# dashboard-api LOGS the verification link instead of sending (dev-friendly).
# Set these for real delivery (works with SES / Postmark / Resend / Gmail / any
# SMTP host). The judge/proxy provider keys above are unrelated to this.
# CASCADIA_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# CASCADIA_SMTP_PORT=587            # 465 => implicit SSL; else STARTTLS
# CASCADIA_SMTP_USER=...
# CASCADIA_SMTP_PASS=...
# CASCADIA_SMTP_FROM=no-reply@yourdomain.com
# CASCADIA_DASHBOARD_URL=https://your-dashboard.example.com  # base for the verify link (default http://localhost:3000)

# ─── Calibration labeling (legacy Basic-Auth vars — no longer gating) ─────
# Superseded by the dashboard auth above; middleware no longer reads these.
# The reviewer_id cookie (labeling attribution) is unaffected.
# CASCADIA_CALIBRATE_USER=cascadia
# CASCADIA_CALIBRATE_PASS=$(openssl rand -hex 12)
# CASCADIA_RUBRIC_PATH=/app/calibration/rubric_v2.md
